<title>USA: AT&amp;T offers rebate on DirecTV RCA system.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T offers rebate on DirecTV RCA system.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>AT&amp;T Corp on Thursday said its long-distance customers who bought a DirecTV satellite system between November 22 and December 1 would receive a $200 rebate, bringing the cost down to $149.</p>
<p>DirecTV is a unit of Hughes Electronics Corp. AT&amp;T bought a 2.5 percent stake in DirecTV for $137.5 million in January. It has the option to increase its stake to 30 percent over five years.</p>
<p>RCA, which supplies the dishes, is owned by Thomson Consumer Electronics, part of Thomson SA of France.</p>
